{"name":"Black Space","hex":"#545354","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"space","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Unlimited or generalized extent, physical or otherwise.\nThe distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, walk, wander.","To set some distance apart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Space","blocks":[{"text":"Black Space is an Israeli TV series, directed by Ofir Lobel. The show's first season started airing in Israel on December 13, 2020, and the second season on June 10, 2024. The first season aired on Netflix globally in May 2021 and the second season aired on Netflix in December 2024."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Space"},{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over whether it is itself an entity, a relationship between entities, or part of a conceptual framework."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/3D_coordinate_system.svg/330px-3D_coordinate_system.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg/500px-Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg/1280px-Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg/500px-Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gottfried Leibniz","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/GodfreyKneller-IsaacNewton-1689.jpg/500px-GodfreyKneller-IsaacNewton-